[{"id":4413235318,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBwygdg","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?u=14b293a7095d074e6653d7ad73269a5e785e1399&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Note that according to the documentation, Jolt's priority works opposite to Godot's priority. Godot:\n\n<img width=\"1580\" height=\"428\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b20895df-8653-4e9c-95f0-48f8ddfe62c2\" />\n\nVs Jolt:\n\n> /// Priority of the constraint when solving. Higher numbers are more likely to be solved correctly.\n\nLooking at the code for GodotPhysics I think the tooltip doesn't describe what actually happens:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/417cd33bf636a0ede02e5e940e963306ea6fc21c/modules/godot_physics_3d/godot_step_3d.cpp#L136-L158\n\nIf I read this code then it will first call `solve()` `iterations` times on each constraint in the current island. Then it will loop and remove all constraints with priority 1. After that it will call `solve()` `iterations` times on the remaining constraints. Then it will loop and remove all constraints with priority 2. etc. This happens until there are no constraints left. So if you set the constraint priority to 1000, then that constraint will actually be solved `1000 * iterations` times, which will be insanely slow. Note that the UI limits the max value to 8, but I think you can set it to any value if you script it. Waht this boils down to is that joints with higher priorities will be solved more accurately.\n\nJolt on the other hand uses the priority only to sort the constraints, so all constraints will be solved `iterations` times, but the highest priority joints are solved last which means that they will be solved more accurately (the first constraints can be violated when solving the last constraints).\n\nI think the tool tip needs to be adjusted to:\n* Reflect that higher values have a higher priority.\n* Remove the note that Jolt doesn't support it.\n\nAs you can pass an int to the `set_solver_priority` function and it is cast to an unsigned integer, I think the value set should be `max(0, value)`.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119976#pullrequestreview-4413235318","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119976","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119976#pullrequestreview-4413235318"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119976"}},"submitted_at":"2026-06-02T20:05:28Z","commit_id":"2209ce840ae6f09021cf07053a7ec7960a70cdcf"},{"id":4420191901,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABB3bGnQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https